   "title": "Where the most snow falls in the next 72 hours: Whistler Blackcomb +74 cm (6 November)",
   "description": "How much snow will the mountains gain? Our table shows the resorts with the most new snow forecast for the next 24 hours and until 9 November, in …",
   "lede": "How much snow will the mountains gain? Our table shows the resorts with the most new snow forecast for the next 24 hours and until 9 November, in Europe, Morocco and North America, with the snow line. For the rivers downstream, how long the snow stays matters as much as how much falls.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "Europe and Morocco",
     "p": [
      "Orcières Merlette (France) should get 0 cm in the next 24 hours and 19 cm within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 2,000 m. For Grindelwald (Switzerland) the forecast gives 4 cm in the next 24 hours and 18 cm in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 2,000 m. La Grave (France) should get 0 cm in the next 24 hours and 15 cm within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 2,900 m."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Against past winters",
     "p": [
      "At about 1,456 m, Whistler has 41 cm today; a normal 6 November has 69 cm there.",
      "Only one winter in ten has more than 125 cm on this date.",
      "A week ago the same spot had 27 cm.",
      "In past winters the best snow at Whistler usually came mid-March / late March."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "United States",
     "p": [
      "For Mt Baker (United States) the forecast gives 2 in (6 cm) in the next 24 hours and 13 in (33 cm) in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 8,200 ft (2,500 m). Hurricane Ridge (United States) should get 0 in (0 cm) in the next 24 hours and 5 in (12 cm) within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 8,200 ft (2,500 m). For Mt. Hood Meadows (United States) the forecast gives 1 in (3 cm) in the next 24 hours and 4 in (10 cm) in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 11,500 ft (3,500 m)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Canada",
     "p": [
      "Whistler Blackcomb (Canada) should get 14 cm in the next 24 hours and 74 cm within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 2,200 m. For Ski Callaghan (Canada) the forecast gives 12 cm in the next 24 hours and 63 cm in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 1,800 m. Mount Cain Alpine Park (Canada) should get 2 cm in the next 24 hours and 50 cm within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 1,800 m."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The next days in the forecast",
     "p": [
      "We place the snow line about 300 m below the forecast freezing level. Above it, the new snow stays dry; below it, wet snow or rain.",
      "Two kinds of numbers here: model estimates for the upper slopes of each resort, and station measurements that are exact but cover one point on the date shown.",
